 "series": {
  "GSE329232": {
   "record": {
    "accession": "GSE329232",
    "title": "Biomarker driven and gene-enhanced virotherapy for malignant peripheral nerve sheath tumor",
    "summary": "Malignant Peripheral Nerve Sheath Tumors (MPNST) are a leading cause of Neurofibromatosis Type 1-related mortality and require targeted interventions. High-grade MPNST is defined by PRC2 loss, which normally represses gene transcription via H3K27me3. We hypothesized that PRC2 loss sensitizes MPNST to oncolytic virotherapy via viral gene transcriptional permissiveness. HSV G47\u0394 sensitivity was investigated using inducible PRC2 rescue, pharmacologic inhibition, and Schwann cell isogenic deletion models. Viability assays, flow cytometry, Cut&Run, and RNA-seq determined viral therapeutic parameters, epigenetic interactions, and resistance mechanisms. Xenografts and syngeneic models assessed in vivo efficacy. All MPNST lines showed a therapeutic window with HSV G47\u0394 versus human Schwann cells. PRC2 deficiency decreased IC50 by approximately 10-fold across all modular systems (p < 0.001). HSV spread after low dose significantly outperforms in the PRC2 deficient context (>95% vs. <10% spread at 72hr, p<0.001), suggesting an early replication advantage. Cut&Run confirmed host histones associate with viral DNA and undergo PRC2-dependent H3K27 trimethylation. However, inadequate viral spread was observed by immunohistochemistry among PRC2-deficient MPNST xenografts. RNA-sequencing of uninfected and infected PRC2 modular systems identified integrated stress response hyperactivation as a key mechanism of resistance, promoting translational arrest and counteracting the benefit of transcriptional permissiveness.",
    "overall_design": "PRC2 modular MPNST models were infected with HSV G47\u00ce\u0094 at sub-lethal, cell line optimized dosing. TY5005 (S462-TY parental) includes a doxycycline inducible SUZ12 cassette to restore H3K27me3. MPNST724 (PRC2 proficient) is pharmacologically pretreated with 1 micromolar valemetostat for 7 days to deplete H3K27me3. N32WT1 (NF1 gene deletion) and N32-3 (NF1 and SUZ12 gene deletions) represent isogenic models derived from hTert immortalized human Schwann cells. Following in vitro infection, flow cytometry (TY5005, MPNST724) or x-gal staining (N32 system) were utilized to quantify percent of live infected cells on technical replicate wells. Cell pellets for 6 biological replicates per group and condition (uninfected and infected) were collected when viral spread was >90% without viability loss to achieve equal viral input. RNA-sequencing reads are quality-filtered and aligned to a hybrid Human (GRCh38) and HSV-1 (Strain F) reference genome using STAR to simultaneously quantify host and viral transcript abundances. Differential expression analysis is performed using host-specific normalization to ensure that changes in the host transcriptome are accurately resolved from dominant viral signatures.",
